  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Data Parallel DDP From Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MiniMLP`: a 3-layer MLP small enough to converge in seconds, large enough to expose the wiring."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `DistributedDataParallel(model, world_size)`: broadcasts params at construct time, returns a wrapper whose `sync_grads` divides accumulated allreduce-summed grads by world_size."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `worker(rank, world_size, ...)`: full training loop with `torch.distributed` init over gloo, forward, backward, sync, step."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `_reference_single_process_loop(...)`: trains the same model on the same data sequentially on one rank, used by the test for byte-equal parameter equivalence after each step."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: a per-step training table comparing single-process loss and parameter checksum to the DDP run on 4 ranks. The two paths produce identical loss curves to float epsilon, proving the gradient sync is correct."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add gradient buckets of configurable size and measure the speedup vs one-allreduce-per-parameter on a deeper model.\n2. Implement `no_sync()` as a context manager and verify gradient accumulation matches a single-process baseline over K microbatches.\n3. Add a `find_unused_parameters` mode where the forward sometimes skips one of the MLP layers; without the flag the run should deadlock.\n4. Replace gloo with `torch.distributed.barrier()`-only synchronisation to feel the difference between allreduce-based and barrier-based sync.\n5. Measure the gradient-sync overhead as a fraction of step time for batch sizes 1, 16, 256 and explain the scaling."
      ]
    }
  ],
